Getsome wrote:
> I was thinking about this today and to me it seems impossible to ascend
> with no wishes / genocides or bones files.
> Has anyone been able to do this regularly?


It is possible and even the preferrable way to play, in my book.

Wishes are usually a matter of convenience.  You can get what you want
in the game if you have the patience and/or luck to find it.   Usually
though it's patience.  Wishes are just a shortcut to getting some item
you're missing from your Kit and are seldom absolute requirements.

Genocide ... I never use it.  It's the first conduct a good players
adopts, for reasons that become clear the more one plays.  The risks it
eliminates do not outweigh the challenges and fun, let's put it that
way.

But, Bones files... I wouldn't eliminate because I think they're the
most interesting element of the game.  For the most part Nethack is
learnable and predictable --  on average, that is.  Seeing what some
other player has left for you to deal with is by far the most
entertaining part.  I love bones files.

Greg.



